{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Mechanical relocation done in worktree (commit e02ab4234258, NOT pushed per operator instruction).\n\ntransport.py: 781 -> 230 LOC. Split into _base.py (157, shared substrate:\nconstruction, _unwrap, _call_logged, _user_attr, _paged_search),\n_issues.py (170, TicketTransport CRUD+labels+transitions), _hierarchy.py\n(156, set_parent/_resolve_epic_link_field_id/get_parent_map),\n_links.py (110, SupportsLinks+SupportsComments co-located - each alone\nfell under the 100-LOC floor), _people.py (177, identity+properties\nco-located for the same reason). transport.py is now the thin\ncomposition root (mixins + build_client_from_settings + probe_remote).\n\nDeviation from the proposed architecture: _comments.py and _properties.py\nas separate files came out at 47 lines each and _links.py at 67 - all\nunder the module-size policy's 100-LOC floor. Merged SupportsComments\ninto _links.py and properties into _people.py; documented the rationale\nin each module's docstring plus the package __init__.py's organising-\nprinciple note.\n\n_resolve_epic_link_field_id extracted as a single method in _hierarchy.py\n(previously inlined in set_parent only; get_parent_map never used it and\nstill doesn't - no behavior added). Reads/writes the epic-link cache via\ngetattr/setattr against _MISSING (not a bare attribute access) - this\nwas ALSO required to work around a real mypy `has-type` limitation when\na mixin inherited from another module reassigns a base-class-declared\nattribute; getattr/setattr resolved both the __new__-skip-init resilience\nconcern and the mypy issue.\n\nGates: make lint, make typecheck, check_comment_hygiene.py all green.\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler (2098) and tests/integration/rebar_reconciler\n(35, -m \"not external\") pass with ZERO test files edited (git show\n--name-only confirms only the 7 non-test files above)."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785802656879464001,"uuid":"b9e074c3-7c88-4766-9a81-5f0e9c385c6c"}